Subject: [LOCAL TEST REFERENCE] include the pinned Raspberry Pi FFmpeg formats

This is a platform-specific golden-reference adaptation, not an upstream mpv
code change. mpv 0.40.0 selects test/ref/ffmpeg7 by libavutil's numeric version;
Raspberry Pi's libavutil 59.39.100 also exposes five downstream formats which
are absent from that upstream reference. Its libavutil/pixfmt.h declares
AVUTIL_HAVE_PIX_FMT_SAND and AV_PIX_FMT_SAND128, AV_PIX_FMT_SAND64_10,
AV_PIX_FMT_SAND64_16, AV_PIX_FMT_RPI4_8 and AV_PIX_FMT_RPI4_10 (lines 442-449).

Provenance: native arm64 libavutil-dev 8:7.1.5-0+deb13u1+rpt2, downloaded using
authenticated APT metadata from archive.raspberrypi.com/debian/pool/main/f/ffmpeg/
libavutil-dev_7.1.5-0%2bdeb13u1%2brpt2_arm64.deb.
Package SHA256: 76f0554065a40cb80929184b5c46a6a34bba106ad21480220a10dd9f1373de66

The native img-format test reached its final reference comparison and aborted
because of exactly this 49-line insertion. All original reference bytes remain
unchanged. The expected additions were reviewed against the matching Pi headers
and generated descriptor output; they must not be generalized to ignore unknown
formats or other differences. Preserve the original failed-test log and rerun
the full suite normally after applying this patch. No failure is suppressed.

